Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Use the regular one-sided normal at a rank-deficient fillet contour end.
TangentExtremity already samples inside an edge when its support has no
normal at the vertex. A numerically defined normal can still be unstable
where the first-derivative cross product is below the existing surface
properties resolution. Reject that endpoint normal and use the same
existing inward samples until the derivatives are regular.

On Apple Silicon the block-on-post lens test's vanishing vertex gave an
angle0.0011074 at cross magnitude1.02e-13, but1.04e-5 just inside the edge
at cross magnitude1.18e-9. The bad endpoint defeated the unchanged5e-4
angular criterion and carried the contour through a zero-width section.
The chain now uses the limiting normal to recognise the tangency there.
No angular tolerance, walking limit, output check or test is relaxed.
The original fillet_lens_overflow test covers this vanishing vertex and
its validity, endpoints, quarter volumes and symmetry; the near-tangent
contour and OCCT cases preserve finite-angle crossings.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 1703.

Upstream: new.
